## 4. Robustness to heaping (48% of 1996 values are multiples of 1,000)
p90/p50 direction, all four specifications:
- A_raw: main +23.70/+25.52 up; p99-winsorised +23.70/+25.52 up; dedup up (dedup A NOT comparable: 94.1% of dropped duplicates were zero rows).
- C_positive: main -1.79/-1.15 down; p99-winsorised -1.79/-1.15 down; dedup -1.68/-1.11 down; nonzero-dedup -1.68/-1.11 down.
-> Within-layer directions fully stable; the A-vs-C flip is a layer-definition effect, not noise.

## 5. ever_jailed control (secondary, association only)
never-jailed whites (n=3,412 WM / 3,618 WF) reproduce the full sample almost exactly:
A p90/p50 13.30->35.66 (WM), 11.88->37.11 (WF); A share w=0 0.257->0.433, 0.202->0.425;
C p90/p50 5.52->3.84, 4.88->3.75; C share top20 0.702->0.639, 0.691->0.617.
Jailed cells: WM n=57 (layer C n_eff 35->25, p90/p50 14.92->4.20), WF n=12 (layer C n_eff 4->3, all ratios NaN).
-> The change is NOT an artifact of the jail subsample. Jailed cells too small to interpret; no causal reading.
No residential-facility / location column exists in the file, so status-at-interview cannot be established.

## 6. Diagnostic (explanatory only, not the estimate)
WM: 675 (19.5%) went wealth>0 -> exactly 0 (their 1990 median 34,700; max 3.5m) vs 108 reverse;
WF: 841 (23.2%) -> 0 (1990 median 41,000) vs 97 reverse. Among always-positive: median +102% (WM) /
+86% (WF), p90 292,180->510,668 / 306,704->508,838. Spearman rank corr 0.539 (WM) / 0.480 (WF);
decile persistence 14.7%/14.8%; top-1% share FELL 0.231->0.182 / 0.221->0.182.
-> The layer-A rise is an **extensive-margin** effect (people leaving the asset-holding class),
not the rich pulling away; among holders the bottom rose fastest.
